# CRLF endings: the value goes before the carriage return.
-- options --
mydumper-version: v0.19.1-2
-- input.cnf.esc --
[mydumper]\r\nroutines\r\n\r\nhost=db\r\n
-- fixed.cnf.esc --
[mydumper]\r\nroutines=1\r\n\r\nhost=db\r\n
-- diagnostics --
2:1-2:9 error MDL113[unsupported-flag-without-value] `routines` has no `=`: mydumper v0.19.1-2 hands the file to GLib without rewriting valueless options into `key= 1` (GLib: Key file contains line “routines” which is not a key-value pair, group, or comment)
  = mydumper ignores this entire file: it only logs a WARNING ("Failed to load config file") and runs with its defaults, exit code 0.
  fix (safe): Write the value explicitly (`routines=1`)
